-- Migration 17 → 18: spray walls (FEAT-078) remember what is still to send or
-- take back. Purely additive.
--
-- head_pending: a published wall's name, angle and gym are in its head event.
-- When only they change, the head goes out on its own; head_pending keeps that
-- until a relay takes it, also across a restart. NULL = nothing to send;
-- otherwise a counter that rises with every such change, so a head that went
-- out clears only the change it was built from.
--
-- withdraw_started: a withdrawal is under way, or a relay took a tombstone of
-- one that did not finish (a photo left on its server, a refused signature). It
-- is set before the first tombstone goes out, so a withdrawal cut off midway
-- keeps it, and cleared when no relay took anything. While it is set the relays
-- may no longer show the wall, so nothing of it is published until the
-- withdrawal is done. NULL = none; otherwise when it started (ms).

ALTER TABLE spray_wall ADD COLUMN head_pending INTEGER;
ALTER TABLE spray_wall ADD COLUMN withdraw_started INTEGER;
